    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 031716\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n916 AM PST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Temperatures will hover within a few degrees of seasonal normals \n  through the week with otherwise quiet conditions.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Monday.\n\nExpect dry conditions, temperatures within a few degrees of\nseasonal normals, and afternoon breeziness through the work \nweek. Shortwave ridging will persist across the Desert Southwest \nfor another day before a weak closed low pushes into the central \nCalifornia Coast and across the Great Basin on Wednesday. Impacts \nfrom this system will be minimal, with only a slight uptick in \nwind speeds across the forecast area (10 to 20 mph gusts in the \nafternoon, with gusts to 25 mph in the higher terrain). Heading \ninto the weekend, heights will increase west-to-east thanks to a \nhigh pressure system in the eastern Pacific Ocean. This will allow\ntemperatures to increase to slightly-above normal. In addition to\nthis ridge, a shortwave will pinch off from the upper-level flow \nand will attempt to close off in the southeastern Pacific. The \nresultant increased pressure gradient across our forecast area \nwill increase northerly wind gusts Friday and Saturday. In \ngeneral, wind speeds will remain sub-advisory, though speeds will \nlikely approach 40 mph in the Colorado River Valley as a result of\nlocalized topographic enhancement. Expect wave heights on Lake \nMohave and Lake Havasu to exceed 2 feet as a result. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill remain light and generally follow typical daily directional \npatterns through the forecast period. SCT-BKN clouds with bases at\nor above 15kft at issuance will gradually clear through this \nafternoon, with clear skies returning this evening onward. VFR \nconditions prevail.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds across the\nregion will generally remain between 5-10KT and follow typical \ndaily directional patterns the next 24 hours. The exceptions \ninclude KBIH in the northern Owens Valley where up-valley winds \nwith gusts to around 20KT develop this afternoon, shifting to the \nnorth-northwest this evening before gusts diminish overnight, \nalong with KDAG in the western Mojave Desert where westerly winds \nare expected to gust to 20-25KT this evening into tonight. SCT-BKN\nclouds with bases around 15-20kft will clear out by this evening,\nwith clear skies thereafter. VFR conditions prevail.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
